    "local_angle": "What drives plumbing problems varies a lot by region: in the Northeast and Midwest, winter freeze-thaw cycles crack pipes and cause bursts (water expands about 9% when it freezes); in the South and especially Texas, expansive clay soil shifts under slab foundations and is a major cause of slab leaks (over 95% of new homes in the West South Central states are built on concrete slabs); and hard-water regions see faster water heater failure and more drain clogs from mineral buildup.",
